{
 "source": "geneva",
 "book": "JOS",
 "chapter": 6,
 "units": [
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.6.1",
   "range": "JOS.6.1",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "47ced7df",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.6.1#p1-fc5afad6",
     "text": "That none could go out.",
     "label": "a"
    },
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.6.1#p2-25c2e3e1",
     "text": "That none could go in.",
     "label": "b",
     "anchor": "shut up"
    },
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.6.1#p3-254709f2",
     "text": "for fear of the Israelites.",
     "label": "c",
     "anchor": "because of the children of Israel"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.6.3",
   "range": "JOS.6.3",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "ced9ec18",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.6.3#p1-ced9ec18",
     "text": "Every day one.",
     "label": "d",
     "anchor": "once"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.6.4",
   "range": "JOS.6.4",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "5a1a9f44",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.6.4#p1-5a1a9f44",
     "text": "That the conquest might not be assigned to man's power, but to the mercy of God, which with most weak things can overcome that which seems most strong.",
     "label": "e",
     "anchor": "rams' horns"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.6.7",
   "range": "JOS.6.7",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "7282e00d",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.6.7#p1-7282e00d",
     "text": "This is chiefly meant by the Reubenites, Gadites, and half the tribe of Manasseh.",
     "label": "f",
     "anchor": "Pass on"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.6.9",
   "range": "JOS.6.9",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "e8237338",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.6.9#p1-e8237338",
     "text": "Meaning, the gathering host, in which was the standard of the tribe of Dan, Nu 10:25.",
     "label": "g",
     "anchor": "rereward came after the ark",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Nu 10:25",
       "ref": "NUM.10.25"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.6.11",
   "range": "JOS.6.11",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "07a0e300",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.6.11#p1-07a0e300",
     "text": "For that day.",
     "label": "h",
     "anchor": "once"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.6.13",
   "range": "JOS.6.13",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "24399b59",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.6.13#p1-24399b59",
     "text": "The tribe of Dan was so called, because it marched last and gathered up whatever was left of others.",
     "label": "i",
     "anchor": "rereward came after the ark of"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.6.15",
   "range": "JOS.6.15",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "75adff33",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.6.15#p1-75adff33",
     "text": "Beside every day once for the space of six days.",
     "label": "k",
     "anchor": "seven times"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.6.17",
   "range": "JOS.6.17",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "2b82447b",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.6.17#p1-2b82447b",
     "text": "That is appointed wholly to be destroyed.",
     "label": "l",
     "anchor": "accursed"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.6.19",
   "range": "JOS.6.19",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "94f755f1",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.6.19#p1-94f755f1",
     "text": "And therefore cannot be put to any private use, but must be first molten, and then serve for the Tabernacle.",
     "label": "m",
     "anchor": "consecrated unto the LORD"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.6.23",
   "range": "JOS.6.23",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "0b579986",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.6.23#p1-0b579986",
     "text": "For it was not lawful for strangers to dwell among the Israelites, till they were purged.",
     "label": "n",
     "anchor": "without the camp of Israel"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.6.24",
   "range": "JOS.6.24",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "33a58938",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.6.24#p1-33a58938",
     "text": "Meaning, the tabernacle.",
     "label": "o",
     "anchor": "house of the LORD"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.6.25",
   "range": "JOS.6.25",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "860be03f",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.6.25#p1-860be03f",
     "text": "For she was married to Salmon prince of the tribe of Judah, Mt 1:5.",
     "label": "p",
     "anchor": "dwelleth in Israel even unto this",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Mt 1:5",
       "ref": "MAT.1.5"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JOS.6.26",
   "range": "JOS.6.26",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "a78a4232",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JOS.6.26#p1-a78a4232",
     "text": "He will build it to the destruction of all his stock, which was fulfilled in Hiel of Beth-el, 1Ki 16:34.",
     "label": "q",
     "anchor": "he shall lay the foundation thereof",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "1Ki 16:34",
       "ref": "1KI.16.34"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
